Schema research contract — agreed shape between research_domain_schema (producer) and create_domain/revise_domain_schema (consumers):

findings[] item: { "topic": "...", "what_is_known": "...", "options": [...], "recommendation": "...", "rationale": "..." }
findings[].options item: { "label": "...", "description": "...", "tradeoffs": "..." }
  — "tradeoffs" is the correct third key in findings options. Do NOT use "value" here.

preference_questions[] item: { "id": "...", "question": "...", "rationale": "...", "affects": "...", "default": "...", "options": [...] }
preference_questions[].options item: { "label": "...", "value": "...", "description": "..." }
  — "value" is the correct second key in preference_questions options. Do NOT use "tradeoffs" here.

A topic that appears in findings cannot also appear in preference_questions.

Workflow research contract — agreed shape between research_workflow_domain (producer) and analyze_and_design_workflow (consumer):

findings[] item: { "topic": "...", "what_is_known": "...", "options": [...], "recommendation": "...", "rationale": "..." }
findings[].options item: { "label": "...", "description": "...", "tradeoffs": "..." }

preference_questions[] item: { "id": "...", "question": "...", "affects": "...", "default": "...", "options": [...] }
preference_questions[].options item: { "label": "...", "value": "...", "description": "..." }

Type 2 gap resolution: findings from right-brain research resolve Type 2 (knowledge) gaps. The left-brain consumer applies findings recommendations directly — they are not surfaced to the user as choices.
